From 7a2525677fe9e46c4c44daf6a9b7e1437dfe8103 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:51:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/54] hw/display/pvg: depth/stencil, unnormalised samplers,
 32-bit stage IO

- DescribeRenderPass depth (bytes 0..39) and stencil (40..75) attachments
  backed by host-only D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT images; SetDepthStencilState
  (PGSerializedDepthStencilDescriptor) and SetStencilRef applied as
  Vulkan 1.3 dynamic state; pipelines keyed by depth/stencil format.
- Unnormalised-coordinate samplers: host samplers stay normalised, air2spv
  divides coordinates by the texture size under spec constant 0 (mask of
  unnormalised sampler slots); pipelines keyed by the masks.
- 8/16-bit vertex inputs, varyings and fragment outputs are declared
  32-bit and converted (storageInputOutput16 is unavailable on NVIDIA).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
